& [Observation] is a live but unregistered remote STDIO tool
  + cantor-attention-mcp is deployed on EVO-X2 and passes official MCP client probes through SSH
  + Codex CLI 0.135.0 supports named STDIO MCP servers launched by a command
  + no configured MCP server currently owns the proposed cantor-attention name

& [Intent] is operator-reviewable Codex registration readiness
  + preserve the exact command that launches the pinned EVO-X2 deployment through noninteractive SSH
  + prove selected and refused route_attention calls over the same transport Codex would launch
  + state tool-use guidance, failure behavior, verification boundary, removal command, and restart requirement
  + keep configuration mutation as an explicit operator decision

& [TrustBoundary] is proposal-only routing
  + registration does not grant signature, authorization, truth, safety, or query_sop authority
  + learned output remains a proposal admitted only after independent evidence verification
  + runtime_busy is terminal for that call and does not authorize automatic retry
  + SSH host trust and EVO-X2 deployment identity remain exterior operator dependencies

& [NonInterference] is mandatory
  + do not alter the existing llama.cpp process or shared sop-agent service
  + do not register, remove, enable, or disable a Codex MCP server during readiness proof
  + do not create a persistent remote process; the STDIO server exits with its client session

& [Deferred] includes actual operator registration, distributed admission, production signing, and broader paraphrase coverage
